            {
              "id": "5b7df72c-f29c-4a84-b504-f867cb551579",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Enjoying It: Candy Crush &amp;  Capitalism</strong></em> was written by Alfie Bown, published by Zero Books, December 11, 2015."
            },
            {
              "id": "f9b4f910-8ff5-4995-ac7a-54767c83e8ad",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "d6220738-fba3-4ea2-a5b9-fd9c56f1bac3",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Using a range of ‘case studies’ from Critical Theory to </em><a href=\"#/candy-crush\">Candy Crush</a><em>, ‘Gangnam Style’ to </em>Game of Thrones<em> and </em><a href=\"#/fortnite\">Football Manager</a><em> to Hieronymus Bosch, this book argues that we need to rethink our enjoyment. Inspired by psychoanalysis, the book offers a new way of thinking about how we talk about what we enjoy and how we enjoy what we talk about.</em>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
